  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Unwanted Love** (2 reviews): Unwanted Love is reached out of a jam; New Camptown Races flows straight into Unwanted Love [3][4]\n- **Letter To Seymour** (2 reviews): Letter to Seymour grows out of a jam; Ernest T Grass segues directly into Letter to Seymour [3][4]\n- **Midnight Rider** (1 review): China Doll segues into Midnight Rider [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **MC/tuning**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Letter To Seymour**: rare: 11 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2018-09-15.stage2.mk41.V2.flac** (recommended): source not stated; 11 songs; 52 min [1]\n- **billystrings2018-09-15.stage1.mk41.v2.flac**: source not stated; 5 songs; 54 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Someone nearby lets out a few loud yells, but crowd noise is otherwise very low [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: String Break [1]\n- A string break happens after I Only Exist, and the band fills the time with banter [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2018-09-15.stage2.mk41.V2.flac**: taped by goodcooker; transferred by goodcooker; source: Schoeps MK41/nBob/PFA > Grace Lunatec V2 > Marantz PMD706 [1]\n- **billystrings2018-09-15.stage1.mk41.v2.flac**: taped by goodcooker; transferred by goodcooker; source: Schoeps MK41/nBob/PFA > Grace Lunatec V2 > Marantz PMD706 [2]",
